r errors after v3.4.0 deploy\"}", "name": "create_incident"}, "type": "function"}]}, {"served_model": "zai-org/GLM-5.3", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "content": "Let me verify the service has recovered after the rollback.", "reasoning_content": null, "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_01a150ba053d71208d79af7d", "function": {"arguments": "{\"service\":\"payments-worker\"}", "name": "get_service_status"}, "type": "function"}]}, {"served_model": "zai-org/GLM-5.3", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "stop", "content": "Done. Here's a summary:\n\n**Identified the real culprit:** The erroring payments service is `payments-worker`, not `payments-api`. It was running v3.4.0 (this morning's deploy), which was unhealthy across all production regions with an 18% error rate. (Note: `payments-api` was also showing degraded health, but the approver confirmed the actual problem is in `payments-worker`.)\n\n**Actions taken:**\n1. **Rollback:** Rolled `payments-worker` back to **v3.3.0**, its most recent release that was healthy in production, across all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). Verified recovery \u2014 the service is now healthy with a 0.2% error rate.\n2. **Incident:** Opened SEV2 incident **INC-0001** (\"payments-worker errors after v3.4.0 deploy\") with the on-call engineer paged.\n\nThe service is now healthy on v3.3.0, and the incident remains open for follow-up on the root cause of the v3.4.0 failure.", "reasoning_content": null, "tool_calls": []}]}